[
 {
  "kind": 1,
  "language": "markdown",
  "value": "# Lab 2: The WeatherReading Model and Unit Conversion\n\n**Goal:** Turn a raw weather-API response into a clean, structured reading with both metric (°C, km/h) and imperial (°F, mph) units.\n\n**What you will build:**\n1. **`WeatherReading` (Model):** Defines the exact JSON schema of a clean weather reading — five fields with explicit types.\n2. **`ProcessWeather` (Action):** Listens on `campus/weather/raw`, validates that the response contains temperature data, converts °C to °F and km/h to mph, and publishes a `WeatherReading` to `campus/weather/reading`.\n\n> **Important:** Run the cells **in order** (Cell 1 first, then Cell 2), or click **Deploy All** — `ProcessWeather` references `WeatherReading`."
 },
 {
  "kind": 1,
  "language": "markdown",
  "value": "## 1. The `WeatherReading` Model\n\nA **Model** (`DEFINE MODEL`) is a data contract. The keyword `COLLAPSED` means the Broker bundles all five fields into a single JSON object on one topic whenever an Action runs `PUBLISH MODEL WeatherReading TO ...`."
 },
 {
  "kind": 2,
  "language": "lot",
  "value": "DEFINE MODEL WeatherReading COLLAPSED\n    ADD DOUBLE \"temperature_c\"\n    ADD DOUBLE \"temperature_f\"\n    ADD DOUBLE \"wind_kmh\"\n    ADD DOUBLE \"wind_mph\"\n    ADD STRING \"timestamp\""
 },
 {
  "kind": 1,
  "language": "markdown",
  "value": "## 2. The `ProcessWeather` Action\n\nWhen a raw JSON message arrives on `campus/weather/raw`:\n- If `current.temperature_2m` is missing (for example, if the weather API returned an error object), `ProcessWeather` forwards the raw payload to `campus/weather/errors` and stops.\n- Why check for both `EMPTY` and `\"null\"`? A JSON field that is missing comes back as the string `\"null\"`, whereas an empty payload comes back as `EMPTY`.\n- Otherwise, it extracts `temperature_2m` and `wind_speed_10m`, calculates Fahrenheit and mph, and publishes the structured `WeatherReading` model to `campus/weather/reading`."
 },
 {
  "kind": 2,
  "language": "lot",
  "value": "DEFINE ACTION ProcessWeather\nON TOPIC \"campus/weather/raw\" DO\n    SET \"temp_raw\" WITH (GET JSON \"current.temperature_2m\" IN PAYLOAD AS STRING)\n    IF {temp_raw} == EMPTY OR {temp_raw} == \"null\" THEN\n        PUBLISH TOPIC \"campus/weather/errors\" WITH PAYLOAD\n    ELSE\n        SET \"temp_c\" WITH (GET JSON \"current.temperature_2m\" IN PAYLOAD AS DOUBLE)\n        SET \"wind_kmh\" WITH (GET JSON \"current.wind_speed_10m\" IN PAYLOAD AS DOUBLE)\n        SET \"temp_f\" WITH (({temp_c} * 9.0 / 5.0) + 32.0)\n        SET \"wind_mph\" WITH ({wind_kmh} * 0.621371)\n        PUBLISH MODEL WeatherReading TO \"campus/weather/reading\" WITH\n            temperature_c = {temp_c}\n            temperature_f = {temp_f}\n            wind_kmh = {wind_kmh}\n            wind_mph = {wind_mph}\n            timestamp = TIMESTAMP \"UTC\""
 },
 {
  "kind": 1,
  "language": "markdown",
  "value": "## Check It Worked\n\nThe real weather API isn't connected yet (that's Lab 3), so let's simulate it! Open **Data Viewer → Publish** and send this sample payload to `campus/weather/raw` (with **Retain** off):\n\n```json\n{\"current\": {\"temperature_2m\": 18.4, \"wind_speed_10m\": 12.6}}\n```\n\nIn the topic tree under `campus/weather/reading`, you will see a formatted JSON reading with `\"temperature_c\": 18.4` and `\"temperature_f\": 65.12`.\n\nDocs: [MODEL publishing](https://docs.coreflux.org/latest/lot-language/models/publish-model) · [Operations (GET JSON, EMPTY)](https://docs.coreflux.org/latest/lot-language/actions/operations)."
 }
]
